SUMMARY:The Climate Commissions
DESCRIPTION:A triple bill\, THE CLIMATE COMMISSIONS explore the climate crisis with workshop presentations of three new short works from critically-acclaimed creators including Tara Beagan\, 2025 Governor General Award for Drama winner\, Sabrina Mahfouz\, an award-winning British writer who grew up in both London and Cairo; and Ta-Nia\, an American-based duo dedicated to creating uncompromising BLK spaces in the theatre. The Climate Commissions is a national and international commission by Why Not Theatre exclusively for the 2025.26 ThisGen Fellowship.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/the-climate-commissions/
LOCATION:The Theatre Centre\, 1115 Queen St. West\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M6J 1J1
CATEGORIES:Theatre & Opera
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/the-climate-commissions.png
END:VEVENT
