SUMMARY:Theatre of Dreams
DESCRIPTION:Theatre of Dreams \nBy Hofesh Shechter Company \nCo-Presented by Luminato Festival and TO Live \nSupported by Kiki and Ian Delaney and Joan and Jerry Lozinski \nWith assistance from TO Live \n \nCurtains open and close\, revealing scenes of spellbinding surrealism where the unexpected unfolds at every turn. As dancers move across the stage\, reality begins to blur—are you witnessing a dream or a nightmare? Theatre of Dreams pulls audiences into a surreal\, unpredictable world where imagination and subconscious collide. \nChoreographed by Hofesh Shechter\, the work blends intricate movement with an electronic sonic score infused with elements of jazz and bossa nova\, creating a soundscape as dynamic and surprising as the dancers themselves. Exploring the chaos of our subconscious\, hopes\, and fears\, the piece offers a mirror into the psyche of humanity—every movement resonating with emotion\, rocked to your core by the music. \nWith lighting design by long-time collaborator Tom Visser\, witness a dreamlike world come alive\, where what you expect is constantly overturned and imagination takes center stage. \nAstonishingly beautiful. Constantly inventive. Utterly engaging. \nContent warning: Some nudity\, haze\, intermittent loud music\, and moments of blackout.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/theatre-of-dreams/
LOCATION:Bluma Appel Theatre\, Bluma Appel Theatre\, 27 Front Street East\, M5E 1B4 Toronto\, Ontario\, Canada\, Toronto\, M5E 1B4
CATEGORIES:Dance,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/theatre-of-dreams-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
